CLT tells--->sampling distribution of a sample mean follows the 
Gaussiaan distribution where the mean is same as population
mean and sd=sd of a population/sqrt(sample_size).

Even if the original data is NOT normal, the distribution of sample means
becomes normal when sample size is large.
The standard deviation of the sample means is called Standard Error.

Formula:se=σ/sqrt(n)​​

